>I'm learning C right now, and I'm trying to figure out how Nethack
>prints things to the terminal.  

include/winprocs.h defines the structure for the procedures to be called.
win/tty/wintty.c defines a function tty_putstr() to write the characters.
Just from the looks of it, most called functions therein have
self-explaining names.

>2. In general, how do you go about finding methods that are being
>called?  

Search in include/extern.h for the function and read at the comments
above the declaration to see in which C file to look. 

